    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0035" n="25" sameAs="frus:frus1948v08/pg25"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/3–148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-03-01T18:00:00-05:00">March 1, 1948—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>322. Supplementary surplus property agreement covering sale aircraft engine
                    overhaul plant equipment Hawaii signed Feb 28 and <pb facs="0036" n="26"
                        xml:id="pg26"/> payment received. (Sent Nanking as 322 repeated Shanghai as
                    370.)</p>
                <p>Movement from Hickam Field depot to port will be made on request of Chinese
                    authorities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
